# Everything in this repository is stored and checked out with LF endings.
#
# This is not a style preference. `tests/truth/` and `tests/parity/` hold
# byte-exact vectors the reference implementation produced, and invariant 2
# makes those bytes a contract. Git's `core.autocrlf` defaults to true on
# Windows, so without this file a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF and the
# interop assertions compare shanon's correct output against a corrupted
# fixture. That is exactly what happened the first time CI ran on
# `windows-latest`.
#
# `eol=lf` and not `text=auto` alone: normalization has to reach the working
# tree, not just the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures and golden vectors are data, not text: never convert them under any
# setting, on any platform, in either direction.
*.json -text
tests/truth/** -text
tests/parity/** -text
